    "slug": "gaza-health-ministry-reports-466-deaths-from-malnutrition-since-2024",
    "summary": "The Gaza Ministry of Health says at least 466 Palestinians, including 157 children and 189 elderly, have died from malnutrition and hunger-related causes since 2024. The announcement came as Gaza marked World Food Day, with hunger conditions still severe in the enclave.",
    "content": "The Gaza Ministry of Health announced on Thursday that at least 466 Palestinians have died from malnutrition and hunger-related complications since the beginning of 2024. Among the deceased are 157 children and 189 individuals over the age of 60, according to the ministry's figures.\n\nThe announcement coincided with World Food Day, drawing attention to the ongoing food crisis in the Gaza Strip. The ministry noted that elderly people accounted for 40.5 percent of all hunger-related deaths, underscoring the particular vulnerability of older residents.\n\nGaza has faced severe food shortages since the conflict escalated in late 2023, with aid deliveries often disrupted and malnutrition rates climbing. International organizations have repeatedly warned of famine-like conditions, particularly in the northern areas of the enclave.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the situation in Gaza resonates deeply. Many Somalis have experienced the devastating effects of famine and conflict firsthand, and the diaspora has historically mobilized to support affected communities. The reported deaths of children and elderly people are likely to heighten concerns among Somali communities about the wider humanitarian impact of the crisis.\n\nAs the world marks World Food Day, the Gaza ministry's figures serve as a stark reminder of the urgent need for sustained humanitarian access. The international community continues to call for increased aid flows to prevent further loss of life.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/17/gaajada-ka-jirta-gaza-oo-sababtay-dhimashada-466-falastiiniyiin-ah-oo-carruur-iyo-waayeello-ay-ku-jiraan/",
