    "content": "On October 16, 2026, the newly elected members of the Galmudug regional parliament were sworn in during a ceremony in Dhuusamareeb. The assembly comprises 89 members chosen to represent communities across the state.\n\nFollowing the swearing-in, Mohamed Sheekh Axmed was appointed as the interim speaker of the Galmudug parliament. He assumed this role by virtue of being the oldest member among the new legislators, a customary practice that allows the eldest member to preside over the chamber until a permanent leadership is elected.\n\nThe interim speaker's primary responsibility is to oversee the selection of the parliament's official leadership. This process is expected to take place in the coming days, with the new speaker and deputy speakers to be chosen by the members.\n\nGalmudug, a federal member state in central Somalia, has been navigating a complex political transition. The election and swearing-in of the new parliament mark a significant step in the state's governance framework. The selection of an interim speaker is a procedural necessity to ensure the orderly conduct of legislative business.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these developments are particularly relevant. Many diaspora members maintain close ties to Galmudug, contributing to its economy and engaging in its political processes. A functioning and representative parliament is seen as crucial for stability and development in the region, which in turn affects diaspora investments and family connections.\n\nThe appointment of an interim speaker is a routine part of parliamentary procedure, but it carries importance as it sets the stage for the election of permanent leadership. The coming days will reveal the direction the new parliament will take under its chosen leadership.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/16/mohamed-sheekh-axmed-oo-noqday-guddoomiyaha-kumeelgaarka-ah-ee-baarlamaanka-galmudug/",
